+Use case: identity-preserve. Edit provided view-front into a single different camera view for a Tripo3D character turnaround. EXACT SAME man, face, short curly dark hair, beard, tan skin, massive thick powerlifter physique with thick belly/thighs, exact black singlet and sleeveless tank, worn dark brown belt with buckle located only at FRONT, black knee sleeves red HORIZONTAL bands at upper/lower edges, black red-striped wrist wraps, calf black socks, black flat shoes. Preserve the SAME physical A-pose: straight upright body, legs shoulder-width apart, arms laterally abducted DOWN 45 degrees in the frontal plane, empty open hands naturally spread fingers. Rotate ONLY camera around vertical axis, do not change physical pose. Realistic scan/photo, soft uniform studio lighting. Uniform solid #d9d9d9 backdrop with NO gradient and NO floor/contact/cast shadow. Entire body centered with uncropped extremities. EXACT same portrait 3:4 canvas and scale as input: topmost hair at y=2.4% and shoe soles at y=95.1% of image, keeping same vertical coordinates for head/shoulders/belt/knees/soles. No text watermark logos props, no barbell. Strict orthographic RIGHT anatomical side profile, camera sees his RIGHT ear and RIGHT body side, nose and all toes point to IMAGE LEFT. In true side projection the laterally spread arms are foreshortened, hands at reference height around hips; do NOT swing arms forward or backward to fake a front-view A silhouette. Feet overlap in profile because they are separated laterally, not staggered.
